ங்கு","lemma":"தங்கு","gloss":"stay"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"past"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you stayed"},{"surface":"சென்மோ","parts":[{"text":"சென்மோ","lemma":"சென்மோ","gloss":"go"}],"gloss":"go","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பாண","parts":[{"text":"பாண","lemma":"பாணன்","gloss":"O bard"}],"gloss":"O bard"},{"surface":"தங்காது","parts":[{"text":"தங்காது","lemma":"தங்கு","gloss":"without stopping"}],"gloss":"without stopping"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேந்து","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"வேந்தன்","gloss":"king"}],"gloss":"king"},{"surface":"தரு","parts":[{"text":"தரு","lemma":"தா","gloss":"given"}],"gloss":"given"},{"surface":"விழு","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"விழு","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"excellent"},{"surface":"கூழ்","parts":[{"text":"கூழ்","lemma":"கூழ்","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"wealth"},{"surface":"பரிசிலர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"பரிசிலர்","lemma":"பரிசிலர்","gloss":"those who receive gifts"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to those who receive gifts"},{"surface":"என்றும்","parts":[{"text":"என்றும்","lemma":"என்றும்","gloss":"always"}],"gloss":"always"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருகாது","parts":[{"text":"அருகாது","lemma":"அருகு","gloss":"without diminishing"}],"gloss":"without diminishing"},{"surface":"ஈயும்","parts":[{"text":"ஈயும்","lemma":"ஈ","gloss":"giving"}],"gloss":"giving"},{"surface":"வண்மை","parts":[{"text":"வண்மை","lemma":"வண்மை","gloss":"generosity"}],"gloss":"generosity"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உரை","parts":[{"text":"உரை","lemma":"உரை","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"சால்","parts":[{"text":"சால்","lemma":"சால்","gloss":"filled with"}],"gloss":"filled with"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தகை","parts":[{"text":"நெடும்","lemma":"நெடு","gloss":"great"},{"text":"தகை","lemma":"தகை","gloss":"noble lord"}],"gloss":"noble lord"},{"surface":"ஓம்பும்","parts":[{"text":"ஓம்பும்","lemma":"ஓம்பு","gloss":"protecting"}],"gloss":"protecting"},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"town"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"town indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the front yard, muññai shrub with mucuṇṭai creeper having grown thickly, / arbor not requiring, under the shade where many rest, / the hunter of wild beasts, in deep sleep having rested, / the decoy young female deer embracing, another / expert in mating solitary male deer enjoying and playing, / seeing that sweet mating posture, the housewife, / fearing her husband waking up, and the male deer / fearing its separating from the female deer, in any way / because of this lack of movement, making a rustling sound, / on the deer skin spread, the drying millet food, / the forest fowl with the quail having seized and eaten, / on the glowing fire, smelling of āral fish, / meat filled and roasted, the whole dried meat, / with your large great family, together pleasantly having eaten, / staying, go, O bard! without stopping, / the king-given excellent wealth, to those who receive gifts, always, / without diminishing, giving generosity, / the famous noble lord protects, this town indeed!","translation":"In the front yard, where the muññai shrub and mucuṇṭai creeper grow so thickly that no thatch is needed, many people rest in the cool shade. The hunter of wild beasts lies there in deep sleep. A solitary buck, expert in love, embraces the decoy doe and sports with her. Seeing their sweet mating, the housewife is filled with fear: she fears her husband might wake up, and she fears the buck might be startled and leave the doe. To prevent any movement that might make a rustling sound, she stands perfectly still. Meanwhile, the forest fowl and quails seize and eat the millet drying on the deer skin. O bard! Eat your fill of the thick, roasted dried meat that smells of āral fish cooked over a glowing fire, along with your large family. Stay a while and then go! This is the town protected by the famous, noble lord who always, without stinting, gives away the excellent wealth bestowed on him by the king to all who seek gifts.","modern":"முற்றத்தில் முஞ்ஞைச் செடியும் முசுண்டைக் கொடியும் அடர்ந்து வளர்ந்து பந்தல் தேவையில்லாதபடி பலர் தங்கும் நிழலைத் தருகின்றன. அங்கே விலங்குகளை வேட்டையாடும் வேட்டுவன் ஆழ்ந்த உறக்கத்தில் இருக்கிறான். அவனுடைய பழக்கப்பட்ட பெண்மானைத் தழுவி, மற்றொரு தனிக் கலைமான் இன்புற்று விளையாடுகிறது. அந்த இனிய புணர்ச்சியைக் கண்ட இல்லத்தரசி, தன் கணவன் விழித்துக்கொள்வான் என்றும், கலைமான் பெண்மானை விட்டுப் பிரிந்து ஓடிவிடும் என்றும் அஞ்சி, சற்றும் அசையாமல் நிற்கிறாள். அவளது அசைவற்ற நிலையால், மான் தோலில் காயப்போட்டிருந்த தினையை காட்டுக்கோழியும் காடையும் வந்து கவர்கின்றன. பாணனே! தழல் நெருப்பில் வாட்டிய, ஆரல் மீன் மணம் வீசும் தசை நிறைந்த உலர்ந்த இறைச்சியை உனது பெரிய சுற்றத்தோடு இனிதாக உண்டு, இங்கே தங்கிவிட்டுப் போவாயாக! மூவேந்தர்கள் தந்த சிறந்த செல்வத்தைப் பரிசிலர்களுக்கு எப்போதும் குறையாமல் வழங்கும் வள்ளல் தன்மை கொண்ட, புகழ்பெற்ற நெடுந்தகை காக்கும் ஊர் இதுவே ஆகும்.","explanation":"A resident of the town is speaking to a traveling bard, inviting him to accept the hospitality of a local chieftain's home. The poem describes the peaceful, abundant life of a warrior's household. The hunter is asleep, a wild buck mates with his decoy doe, and the housewife stands frozen in empathy so as not to disturb them, even as birds eat her drying millet. This belongs to the vākai tiṇai, specifically vallāṇ mullai, which praises the strength and domestic virtue of a brave warrior. The domestic scene highlights the tenderness of the warrior's wife, who values the love of the deer over her own drying grain. The abundance of meat and the chieftain's unstinting generosity show the prosperity of the land. Key words include neṭuntakai (noble lord), vaṇmai (generosity), maṉaiyōḷ (housewife), and pāṇa (O bard).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.5],[1.5,1.75],[1.8,2.35],[2.35,2.9],[2.9,3.6],[3.6,3.8],[3.8,4.17],[4.17,5.08],[5.08,6.0],[6.0,6.5],[6.5,7.3],[7.3,7.6],[7.6,8.3],[8.3,8.5],[8.5,9.8],[9.8,10.3],[10.3,10.6